{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1535886-roads-and-paths-for-requiem","id":1535886,"title":"Roads and Paths for Requiem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-18T23:43:34-07:00","id":1535886,"title":"Roads and Paths for Requiem","content":"Exactly what it says. <br /> <br /> Has someone tried to port this element of Masquerade to Requiem just as people try and port the Clan?<br /> <br /> I'm toying with the idea of super-banes one can take to adopt alternate sins against Humanity. Take a permanent Bestial condition for the Road of the Beast by instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T06:49:00-07:00","id":1535901,"title":"","content":"Never really delved into the subject, though i did think once or twice of doing them in a format like a martial arts &quot;merit tree&quot; or the Mind of the Devouring Worm/Unblinking Serpent/Inscrutable Hydra &quot;pseudo-coil&quot; (my words, not theirs) in the OD book.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-19-2024, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T14:24:01-07:00","id":1535922,"title":"","content":"The problem is that Requiem has already the Banes rule, plus a different understanding of Humanity, where it is as much a marker of how you understand the prey as it is a buffer against the Beast.<br /> <br /> Given how Paths work, and how Banes already work, I have an idea:<br /> <br /> A Path is a Merit that work exactly like Touchstone, but instead of people the extra Touchstones are the rules of the Path, while the prerequisite for a given Path is to take specific Breaking Points for your Banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 05-19-2024, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-19T15:54:28-07:00","id":1535928,"title":"","content":"I don't remember if this was covered in the Translation Guide. Even if it was, that would have been 1st ed VtR","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T11:51:20-07:00","id":1536074,"title":"","content":"We never tried using paths or roads in any VTR games we ever played, but then again we were never fans of the paths of enlightenment in general. But if you can make it work in your games then go ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T18:57:40-07:00","id":1536089,"title":"","content":"I liked it when NWoD came out with no paths as I disagreed with the roads and always though Humanity should be the only path. <br /> <br /> Even for the Sabbat; yes, they do horrible things and will lose Humanity, but that's why they're all young right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T19:48:45-07:00","id":1536091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1535886-roads-and-paths-for-requiem?p=1536089#post1536089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked it when NWoD came out with no paths as I disagreed with the roads and always though Humanity should be the only path.<br /> <br /> Even for the Sabbat; yes, they do horrible things and will lose Humanity, but that's why they're all young right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, unless one uses a very peculiar definition of &quot;all young&quot;. That's kind of like a living, breathing human in the present saying &quot;newfangled communism/soviet union&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T20:32:08-07:00","id":1536092,"title":"","content":"While I'm normally a much bigger fan of the Pathes, I haven't considered adopting them over, I like how humanity works in Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T12:57:56-07:00","id":1537876,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be shocked if some players tried to create paths as a merit of some sort during the time when VTR was introduced, but honestly I wouldn't know how to to make one and we didn't have any interest in making any. It was Bloodlines or Devotions that took up our focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T06:27:05-07:00","id":1538231,"title":"","content":"I did a half-assed attempt way back in 1ed, if I recall.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe basic idea was that you bought a merit which was essentially an ethic from a Road/Path. If you then did a sin against Humanity but the act was in accordance with this merit's ethic you got a bonus to your Humanity roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T22:41:37-07:00","id":1539736,"title":"","content":"I feel the Roads and Paths run fundamentally contrary to what Requiem is about.<br /> <br /> In theory, they should be about making your Vampire more detached from mortal morals and values and truly become that tragic creature that has become a monster but cling to an insane logic to try and preserve a sense of sanity. It shouldn't be exhilerating to be on a Road or a Path, it should be horrific because the only means your Vampire has found a way to preserve his sense of self is to basically discard almost anything that was him to begin with.<br /> <br /> But in practice, it was (is) mostly a way to be as monstrous as one wants without the consequences. And it can sort of work in Mascarade, what with the Jyhad and the Antediluvians and what not. <br /> <br /> In Requiem however, I feel like personnal horror is far more developped and it means something. When one pursue Cru\u00e0c to rise in the ranks of the Circle, they sacrifice that precious Humanity for more power, but it's still possible to retain enough of it that you can sort of function around mortals still, yet you still have bartered a precious ressource for power and you need to live with that, for instance. If it was possible to just say &quot;my Path basically means Cru\u00e0c is okay so I can be whatever level I want on it with the strongest rituals&quot; something would be lost to me.<br /> <br /> And it's generally the same for everything else in the game. We are only humans, we can only fully comprehend the world as a human and it means that the Roads and Paths can't gripe us as viscerally as having our Vampire killing someone in cold-blood and seen ruminating and suffering mentally because she feels she's slipping further away from whom she was and how can she now see her mortal best friend next night if she's that dangerous ? <br /> <br /> TLDR : The slippery slope in Requiem is far more affirmed to me than it is in Mascarade and the Roads and Paths remove it in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T08:01:00-07:00","id":1539749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1535886-roads-and-paths-for-requiem?p=1539736#post1539736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the Roads and Paths run fundamentally contrary to what Requiem is about.<br /> <br /> In theory, they should be about making your Vampire more detached from mortal morals and values and truly become that tragic creature that has become a monster but cling to an insane logic to try and preserve a sense of sanity. It shouldn't be exhilerating to be on a Road or a Path, it should be horrific because the only means your Vampire has found a way to preserve his sense of self is to basically discard almost anything that was him to begin with.<br /> <br /> But in practice, it was (is) mostly a way to be as monstrous as one wants without the consequences. And it can sort of work in Mascarade, what with the Jyhad and the Antediluvians and what not.<br /> <br /> In Requiem however, I feel like personnal horror is far more developped and it means something. When one pursue Cru\u00e0c to rise in the ranks of the Circle, they sacrifice that precious Humanity for more power, but it's still possible to retain enough of it that you can sort of function around mortals still, yet you still have bartered a precious ressource for power and you need to live with that, for instance. If it was possible to just say &quot;my Path basically means Cru\u00e0c is okay so I can be whatever level I want on it with the strongest rituals&quot; something would be lost to me.<br /> <br /> And it's generally the same for everything else in the game. We are only humans, we can only fully comprehend the world as a human and it means that the Roads and Paths can't gripe us as viscerally as having our Vampire killing someone in cold-blood and seen ruminating and suffering mentally because she feels she's slipping further away from whom she was and how can she now see her mortal best friend next night if she's that dangerous ?<br /> <br /> TLDR : The slippery slope in Requiem is far more affirmed to me than it is in Mascarade and the Roads and Paths remove it in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, this summarizes most of my thoughs perfectly.<br /> <br /> I feel that Roads and Paths were a blantant scope creep in the VtM books, too many bloodlines, character options, etc... Most likely due to the inexperience of the writters in creating verosimilitude, the lack of real baseline document describing what VtM was about among writters, and the general edginess of the 90's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T09:42:01-07:00","id":1539754,"title":"","content":"That's a good description of the Paths of Enlightenment as any I heard Ur-Than and why it wouldn't fit in the Vampire The Requiem setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T10:42:27-07:00","id":1539757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1535886-roads-and-paths-for-requiem?p=1539736#post1539736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But in practice, it was (is) mostly a way to be as monstrous as one wants without the consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>With time I've learned to understand and accept Paths as a part of the game in Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The game has many ways to be played, and Paths do imply an effort. Are they an excuse to do what you wanted all along? I find this to be a very weak argument, and I say this as someone that almost never stray from Humanity, yet I can thoroughly say it <b>is </b>a &quot;Path of doing what I would do anyway&quot; for me.<br /> <br /> Personal horror is just one aspect of the game, and as much as I like it, it is and should be totally optional. Otherwise it's just being an a-hole with the &quot;bad&quot; players to punish their &quot;badwrongfun&quot;.<br /> <br /> My reason to not see the need of Paths in Requiem has more to do with 2nd Edition doing the job through Banes. I find it in general a more interesting mechanic, specially with the non moral take on Humanity.<br /> <br /> But if someone still feels the need for Paths to make some character concept, so be it. In my own table I would be glad to work it around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T13:27:01-07:00","id":1539764,"title":"","content":"If you want Paths to<i> sort of</i> work, have Path followers take a Support Network (Hurt Locker) representing a club or a singular guru who tells your character &quot;No, what you did was right.&quot;<br /> Or just be Invictus and take Noblesse Oblige. That's pretty much a step onto the Road of Kings all by itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T08:54:41-07:00","id":1539857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1535886-roads-and-paths-for-requiem?p=1539757#post1539757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With time I've learned to understand and accept Paths as a part of the game in Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The game has many ways to be played, and Paths do imply an effort. Are they an excuse to do what you wanted all along? I find this to be a very weak argument, and I say this as someone that almost never stray from Humanity, yet I can thoroughly say it <b>is </b>a &quot;Path of doing what I would do anyway&quot; for me.<br /> <br /> Personal horror is just one aspect of the game, and as much as I like it, it is and should be totally optional. Otherwise it's just being an a-hole with the &quot;bad&quot; players to punish their &quot;badwrongfun&quot;.<br /> <br /> My reason to not see the need of Paths in Requiem has more to do with 2nd Edition doing the job through Banes. I find it in general a more interesting mechanic, specially with the non moral take on Humanity.<br /> <br /> But if someone still feels the need for Paths to make some character concept, so be it. In my own table I would be glad to work it around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Paths certainly works in Mascarade overall, and there is little reason not to use them. When I played a chronicle of VTM, I did lean into them myself.<br /> <br /> But for Requiem proper I feel they'd undermine too much of the building blocks of the game. From the various curses and banes to the Stryx, too much of what makes Requiem distinct from its predecessor would be lost if Paths were just introduced piecemeal. <br /> <br /> The Birds of Dis introduction in 2ed made clear that the core conflict of the setting is Man vs the Beast in a way that wasn't the case in Mascarade as the Stryx want to punish the Kindred to not having killed the Man yet. For clinging to morality, of any kind, instead of embracing the wickedness of their condition. <br /> <br /> And even before them, Belial's Brood also had that sort of idea, even if not as purely distilled than the Owls. And that's only because the setting has been built on ideas and thematics antithetics to the Paths and Roads that I don't feel they fit in Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-08T15:11:44-08:00","id":1557388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1535886-roads-and-paths-for-requiem#post1535886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly what it says.<br /> <br /> Has someone tried to port this element of Masquerade to Requiem just as people try and port the Clan?<br /> <br /> I'm toying with the idea of super-banes one can take to adopt alternate sins against Humanity. Take a permanent Bestial condition for the Road of the Beast by instance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Belial's Brood</b> has <i>The Pursuit</i>, which (to hear them tell it) is supposed to culminate in the vampire completely erasing their Humanity, while still retaining control over themselves. They don't see the Beast as a pervasive, overriding force that struggles to take control. They view it as an extension of their own dark soul, and one which a true vampire should strive to be more in lined with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}